Q. What does a splitter do? What is the differance between General splitter and Iterative splitter?
A. In SAP CPI, a splitter breaks down a large message into smaller, individual messages for processing.
   The main difference between a General Splitter and an Iterating Splitter lies in how they handle the parent
   nodes or enclosing tags of the split messages.
   General Splitter:
   ----------------
   Preserves the header or root element of the composite message in each individual split message.
   Includes the encapsulating elements (e.g., <Products> in the example) in each split chunk.

   If you have a message like <Products><Product><Id>1</Id><Name>Biscuit</Name></Product></Products>,
   the General Splitter might output <Products><Product><Id>1</Id><Name>Biscuit</Name></Product></Products>
   for each split message.

   Iterating Splitter:
   ------------------
   Splits the message into individual messages but doesn't include the encapsulating elements of the composite message.
   Effectively extracts the desired elements from the message, leaving out the surrounding tags.

   The Iterating Splitter might output <Product><Id>1</Id><Name>Biscuit</Name></Product> for each split message,
   essentially removing the <Products> tag.

