Q.SAH VS RSA
RSA and SHA are fundamental cryptographic tools, but they serve different purposes. RSA is an asymmetric
encryption algorithm used for secure key exchange and digital signatures, while SHA is a cryptographic
hash function used to verify data integrity. RSA uses key pairs (public and private) for encryption and
decryption, while SHA generates a unique "fingerprint" (hash) of data that can't be reversed to the original data.
